--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. MECHANISM: primitive_uv_sphere_add shuffles its face order per call.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Probe: 5 consecutive bpy.ops.mesh.primitive_uv_sphere_add(radius=1, loc=origin)
calls in ONE `blender --background --python` process; per call we hash
(a) vertex coords in vertex order, (b) polygon vertex-indices in polygon order,
(c) the polygon list as a sorted multiset.

segments=14 ring_count=9   -> verts=114 faces=126   (the minimal repro quoted
  in the comment) face-order hashes over 5 calls:
    ed3695e7f3a77ecc a33708822030f706 26781a4d9d8581cb e92ff2e20c1d6fe8
    11cebe858f126118                          -> 5 distinct orders / 5 calls
segments=20 ring_count=12  (the ball() default profile) verts=222 faces=240:
  first run: 4 distinct orders / 5 calls, second run: 5 / 5
  (66c659d00a02891d b26f658eb37f4cd2 3e96979289320867 3e96979289320867
   18770e3e6e81bcd8)
In every case: vertex coords identical in vertex order, and the face multiset
identical; ONLY the emission order of the polygons moves.

Same test, 5 calls each, order-STABLE (1 distinct order / 5):
  primitive_ico_sphere_add(subdivisions=2)  8309d39b935cd8c8 x5
  primitive_torus_add(32x8)                 b09c7afc029757db x5
  primitive_cylinder_add(20)                6e9b005281930af2 x5
  primitive_cone_add(20)                    6e9b005281930af2 x5
  primitive_cube_add(size=2)                e1d691c918ec5ccb x5
  primitive_plane_add(size=2)               5a3e8669f334916f x5

bmesh.ops.create_uvsphere(u_segments=20, v_segments=12) shuffles too:
  5 calls -> 5 distinct polygon orders. So it is the UV-sphere polygon
  emission itself, not the operator wrapper.

Repro:  blender --background --python <probe with the loops above>
(the probe scripts live in /tmp/rsb95/uv_repro*.py of the measuring session;
 the exact call parameters are stated inline and are deterministic to rerun).

