2. PARITY: launch_tower built TWICE at HEAD vs TWICE with canon_polys().
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Command shape (run from the repo root; asset arg must be the builder's real
stage path, build_base_v2 exports to OUT=/tmp/rsb_stage3, not public/):

  python3 tools/glb_repro_pair.py /tmp/rsb_stage3/launch_tower.glb -- \
      blender --background --python <copy>/tools/blender/build_base_v2.py -- launch_tower

<copy> = /tmp/rsb95/head (git archive of HEAD tools/blender) and
         /tmp/rsb95/work (working tree incl. canon_polys). rc per run = 0.

AT HEAD (canon_polys absent) — two builds of the SAME script byte-DIFFER:
  run1 4710656 B sha256 a42df235ec0557e6cc6ed5034c3f9af25e735bbd2e08e1626ed268d391bf1855
  run2 4710656 B sha256 f0a939e414b70398c0ffb1e1ecb45dd84426e2bf3746a37cf1a9d49bb6171765
  JSON chunk equal; differing bytes: SCALAR/ELEMENT_BUFFER (triangle indices)
  10593 + VEC2 TEXCOORD 98 (<=4 ULP).  -> REPRO_PAIR_INDEX_DRIFT, pair rc=1

WITH canon_polys APPLIED — index drift GONE, but still not byte-identical:
  run1 4710656 B sha256 982febb45123f918e28b40001e9b8a62cf2e3bfbfef0d89e4905fd62ddd7a185
  run2 4710656 B sha256 05f1ebcaabc242c34e988854b7ae5aa425c7ddd1f853c9df00bafd9383671306
  JSON equal; differing bytes: VEC2 TEXCOORD only, 66 (<=4 ULP), indices
  byte-identical.  -> REPRO_PAIR_FLOAT_DRIFT, pair rc=3
  The residual is the bmesh.ops.bevel(clamp_overlap=True) UV-interpolation
  order documented in tools/glb_repro_pair.py header; canon_polys cannot pin
  it and no builder-side fix for it is claimed.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. GEOMETRY: canon_polys moves buffer bytes only, not the shape.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
head run1.glb vs canon run1.glb: JSON chunks byte-EQUAL; only SCALAR index
accessors (29508 B) and VEC2 TEXCOORD (248 B) differ; POSITION and NORMAL
accessors byte-identical; winding preserved (canon sorts whole vertex-index
tuples verbatim).

head/canon rebuilds vs the IN-REPO public/assets/launch_tower.glb (4710836 B):
  shipped: tris=91636 verts=129456 JSON sha dd67fdd6341077e5
  rebuild: tris=91636 verts=129450 JSON sha 9ed4b35801769fef
  POSITION bbox identical: min [-10.81873,-2.535,-3.135] max [9.9,51.82,3.8]
  (exporter y-up space). The shipped asset therefore predates the current
  script by a real content delta (6 verts, different JSON) that is present in
  BOTH HEAD rebuilds and is NOT caused by canon_polys. A regenerated
  launch_tower.glb is needed either way; with canon_polys the regeneration is
  at least reproducible up to the 66-byte UV float drift.

